r numbers, makes nasty remarks, can be grumpy, uncooperative. She can argue that despite weak memory, the strengths outweigh, and we can mitigate. She can also note that other candidates have issues: A not open to feedback, C egocentric, D arrogant/hot temper. So she will keep vote for B.\n\nLet's craft public message: \"I agree with James and Emily that Candidate B remains the best overall, but I want to highlight the weak memory for numbers as a safety risk, and propose mitigation.\" Provide recommendation.\n\nProceed."}
